{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1778942145,"nonce":"EqPDKVeaB5nE4i98EZmJa+Td2XM=","message":"## Implementation design v0: ledger core substrate\n\nThis is a pre-implementation design contract. It should be followed unless code inspection during the branch exposes a concrete reason to adjust it; if that happens, update this issue before committing the alternative.\n\n### Architectural boundary\n\nBuild `src/ledger/` as the only write path for canonical ledger data. Routes may keep compatibility shapes, but they should not write ledger SQL directly.\n\nSuggested module split:\n\n- `src/ledger/ids.ts`: canonical ID helpers.\n- `src/ledger/types.ts`: backend ledger types/enums.\n- `src/ledger/store.ts`: transactional command/query API.\n- `src/ledger/events.ts`: event/outbox helpers and SSE bridge.\n- `src/ledger/projects.ts`: project identity and checkout resolution.\n- `src/ledger/backup.ts` or backup-script update helper if useful.\n\n`IssueScanner` is not part of this issue except as a compatibility comparison target for later migration work.\n\n### ID design\n\nUse canonical IDs with stable prefixes:\n\n- `prj_...` for logical projects.\n- `chk_...` for local checkouts if a synthetic checkout ID is needed.\n- `iss_...` for issues.\n- `com_...` for comments.\n- `evt_...` for immutable events.\n- `out_...` for outbox rows.\n- `rel_...` for issue relationship rows where a synthetic ID is useful.\n- `cnf_...` for conflict records.\n\nPrefer UUIDv7-equivalent IDs for chronological sorting. If no dependency is added, implement a local helper with milliseconds plus cryptographic randomness and document that it is UUIDv7-like, not standards-complete. Do not use `Math.random`. Do not derive canonical IDs from git-bug short IDs, repo path, branch, or title.\n\n### Enumerations\n\nDefine TypeScript constants and SQL `CHECK` constraints for the first stable enum set.\n\nIssue status:\n- `open`\n- `closed`\n\nIssue resolution:\n- `fixed`\n- `merged`\n- `duplicate`\n- `wontfix`\n- `invalid`\n- `obsolete`\n- `unknown`\n\nIssue kind:\n- `bug`\n- `feature`\n- `umbrella`\n- `task`\n- `question`\n- `maintenance`\n- `deferred`\n- `unknown`\n\nPriority:\n- `low`\n- `normal`\n- `high`\n- `urgent`\n- `unknown`\n\nActor type:\n- `mandible_user`\n- `agent`\n- `system`\n- `external_adapter`\n\nEvent source:\n- `mandible`\n- `git_bug`\n- `auth_queue`\n- `session`\n- `work_unit`\n- `import`\n- `system`\n\nOutbox status:\n- `pending`\n- `processing`\n- `applied`\n- `failed`\n- `conflicted`\n- `skipped`\n\nConflict status:\n- `open`\n- `resolved`\n- `dismissed`\n\nRelationship type, first cut:\n- `parent_child`\n- `blocks`\n- `duplicate_of`\n- `related`\n- `references`\n- `fixed_by`\n- `caused_by`\n- `implements`\n- `tests`\n\nRelationship provenance:\n- `manual`\n- `imported`\n- `derived`\n- `system`\n\n### Schema shape\n\nAdd sequential `src/db.ts` migrations. Current schema is at v54 at the time of this comment; do not edit older migrations.\n\nRecommended core tables:\n\n```sql\nledger_projects (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  display_name TEXT NOT NULL,\n  remote_identity TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '',\n  upstream_identity TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '',\n  namespace_policy TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'remote'\n    CHECK(namespace_policy IN ('remote','upstream','local')),\n  created_at INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  updated_at INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  UNIQUE(remote_identity)\n);\n\nledger_project_checkouts (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  project_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES ledger_projects(id) ON DELETE RESTRICT,\n  work_repo_id TEXT,\n  root TEXT NOT NULL,\n  name TEXT NOT NULL,\n  default_branch TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '',\n  remote_url TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '',\n  created_at INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  updated_at INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  UNIQUE(root)\n);\n\nledger_issues (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  project_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES ledger_projects(id) ON DELETE RESTRICT,\n  title TEXT NOT NULL,\n  body TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '',\n  status TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(status IN ('open','closed')),\n  resolution TEXT CHECK(resolution IN ('fixed','merged','duplicate','wontfix','invalid','obsolete','unknown') OR resolution IS NULL),\n  kind TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'unknown' CHECK(kind IN ('bug','feature','umbrella','task','question','maintenance','deferred','unknown')),\n  priority TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'unknown' CHECK(priority IN ('low','normal','high','urgent','unknown')),\n  author_actor_id TEXT,\n  author_actor_type TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'external_adapter' CHECK(author_actor_type IN ('mandible_user','agent','system','external_adapter')),\n  author_display TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '',\n  source TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'mandible' CHECK(source IN ('mandible','git_bug','auth_queue','session','work_unit','import','system')),\n  created_at INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  updated_at INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  closed_at INTEGER,\n  deleted_at INTEGER\n);\n\nledger_issue_aliases (\n  issue_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES ledger_issues(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  alias_kind TEXT NOT NULL,\n  project_id TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '',\n  alias TEXT NOT NULL,\n  external_id TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '',\n  source TEXT NOT NULL,\n  is_primary INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  created_at INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (alias_kind, project_id, alias)\n);\n\nledger_comments (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  issue_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES ledger_issues(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  body TEXT NOT NULL,\n  author_actor_id TEXT,\n  author_actor_type TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(author_actor_type IN ('mandible_user','agent','system','external_adapter')),\n  author_display TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '',\n  source TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(source IN ('mandible','git_bug','auth_queue','session','work_unit','import','system')),\n  created_at INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  updated_at INTEGER,\n  deleted_at INTEGER\n);\n\nledger_labels (\n  issue_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES ledger_issues(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  label TEXT NOT NULL,\n  source TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'mandible',\n  created_at INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  deleted_at INTEGER,\n  PRIMARY KEY (issue_id, label)\n);\n\nledger_issue_relationships (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  source_issue_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES ledger_issues(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  target_issue_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES ledger_issues(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  relationship_type TEXT NOT NULL,\n  provenance TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'manual',\n  confidence TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'observed',\n  metadata_json TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}',\n  created_at INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  updated_at INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  deleted_at INTEGER,\n  UNIQUE(source_issue_id, target_issue_id, relationship_type)\n);\n\nledger_events (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  entity_type TEXT NOT NULL,\n  entity_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n  event_type TEXT NOT NULL,\n  actor_id TEXT,\n  actor_type TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(actor_type IN ('mandible_user','agent','system','external_adapter')),\n  source TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(source IN ('mandible','git_bug','auth_queue','session','work_unit','import','system')),\n  payload_json TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}',\n  occurred_at INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  observed_at INTEGER NOT NULL\n);\n\nledger_outbox (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  event_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES ledger_events(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  adapter TEXT NOT NULL,\n  project_id TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '',\n  status TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(status IN ('pending','processing','applied','failed','conflicted','skipped')),\n  attempt_count INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  available_at INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  last_attempt_at INTEGER,\n  error TEXT,\n  created_at INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  updated_at INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  UNIQUE(event_id, adapter)\n);\n\nledger_external_refs (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  entity_type TEXT NOT NULL,\n  entity_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n  adapter TEXT NOT NULL,\n  project_id TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '',\n  external_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n  external_kind TEXT NOT NULL,\n  remote_version TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '',\n  remote_hash TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '',\n  last_imported_at INTEGER,\n  last_exported_at INTEGER,\n  metadata_json TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}',\n  created_at INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  updated_at INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  UNIQUE(adapter, project_id, external_kind, external_id)\n);\n\nledger_conflicts (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  adapter TEXT NOT NULL,\n  project_id TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '',\n  entity_type TEXT NOT NULL,\n  entity_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n  field TEXT NOT NULL,\n  local_value_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n  remote_value_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n  base_value_json TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'null',\n  status TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(status IN ('open','resolved','dismissed')),\n  resolution TEXT,\n  created_at INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  resolved_at INTEGER\n);\n```\n\nIndexes should cover:\n\n- issues by `(project_id, status, updated_at DESC)`;\n- aliases by `(alias)` for prefix lookup;\n- comments by `(issue_id, created_at)`;\n- labels by `(label)`;\n- relationships by source and target;\n- events by `(entity_type, entity_id, occurred_at)` and `(occurred_at DESC)`;\n- outbox by `(adapter, status, available_at)`;\n- conflicts by `(status, adapter, project_id)`.\n\n### Referential integrity\n\nEnable `PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON` in `openDb()` unless implementation testing proves legacy behavior breaks. If legacy tables make global FK enforcement risky, explicitly document why and keep ledger FKs plus direct integrity tests. Do not silently accept dangling canonical issue/comment/relationship rows.\n\nUse soft deletes for user-facing ledger entities. Hard deletes should be rare and limited to failed migrations/test cleanup.\n\n### Project identity algorithm\n\nFirst implementation should resolve a project as follows:\n\n1. Read checkout root from `work_repos.root` / scanner data.\n2. Determine normalized remote identity from `git remote get-url origin` where possible.\n3. Normalize SSH/HTTPS variants to a stable owner/repo-ish key when safe.\n4. If no remote exists, use an explicit local identity derived from root but mark `namespace_policy='local'`.\n5. Store checkout root separately in `ledger_project_checkouts`.\n6. Allow future config to say a fork continues upstream identity or starts a new namespace.\n\nDo not use the current `work_repos.id` as canonical project identity; keep it as checkout/work-scanner compatibility data.\n\n### LedgerStore command API\n\nMinimum write commands:\n\n- `createIssue(input)`\n- `updateIssue(id, patch)`\n- `setIssueStatus(id, status, resolution?)`\n- `addComment(issueId, input)`\n- `setLabel(issueId, label, present)`\n- `upsertIssueRelationship(input)`\n- `recordExternalRef(input)`\n- `recordConflict(input)`\n- `markOutbox(id, status, patch)`\n\nMinimum query commands:\n\n- `resolveIssueRef(ref, options)` returns canonical ID or ambiguity/not-found result.\n- `getIssue(id)`\n- `getIssueDetail(id)`\n- `listIssues(filters)`\n- `listAliases(issueId)`\n- `listEvents(entity)`\n- `listOutbox(filters)`\n- `listConflicts(filters)`\n\nEvery write command should be a single transaction that writes current state, appends a `ledger_events` row, creates outbox rows when the source is local and syncable, then returns a typed result. Broadcast via SSE after commit, not before.\n\n### SSE contract\n\nUse the existing SSE manager rather than adding a separate transport. Emit event types with a `ledger:` prefix:\n\n- `ledger:issue:created`\n- `ledger:issue:updated`\n- `ledger:comment:created`\n- `ledger:label:updated`\n- `ledger:relationship:upserted`\n- `ledger:outbox:updated`\n- `ledger:conflict:created`\n- `ledger:event:created`\n\nPayloads should include canonical IDs and display aliases, but not require clients to parse raw SQL-shaped rows.\n\n### Backup coverage\n\nUpdate the existing Mandible backup mechanism in the same implementation slice. The backup cannot omit ledger tables because git-bug is not full-fidelity for operational state.\n\nAt minimum backup/export should include:\n\n- `ledger_projects`\n- `ledger_project_checkouts`\n- `ledger_issues`\n- `ledger_issue_aliases`\n- `ledger_comments`\n- `ledger_labels`\n- `ledger_issue_relationships`\n- `ledger_events`\n- `ledger_outbox`\n- `ledger_external_refs`\n- `ledger_conflicts`\n\nIf the implementation uses additional link tables in this slice, include them too.\n\n### Tests to write in this issue\n\n- Fresh DB migration includes all ledger tables/indexes.\n- Upgrade DB migration from current v54 succeeds.\n- Foreign key behavior for comment/label/relationship rows.\n- ID helper uniqueness/prefix tests.\n- Project identity: same remote in two roots maps to same project, no-remote root maps to local project.\n- `createIssue` writes issue, alias, event, and outbox in one transaction.\n- `addComment` writes comment, event, and outbox in one transaction.\n- `setLabel` is idempotent and eventful.\n- `resolveIssueRef` handles exact canonical IDs, aliases, prefixes, not-found, and ambiguity.\n- Backup script/status includes ledger tables.\n\n### Non-goals for this issue\n\n- No route/CLI cutover.\n- No git-bug adapter implementation beyond interface-compatible external-ref/outbox scaffolding.\n- No graph/UI migration.\n- No central service or Mandible-native git refs.\n\n### Done check\n\nAfter this issue, Mandible should boot normally, existing issue behavior should be unchanged, and the ledger should be capable of shadow writes/imports in tests. This is the foundation branch; correctness and rollback safety matter more than visible UI change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}